## Almond or Coffin: The Decision Framework (Choose Your Shape in Under Two Minutes)

The answer to <strong>coffin nails vs almond nails</strong> is not personal preference. It is a function of your hands, your length, and what you plan to put on your nails. Here is how it resolves.

**Choose almond if:**
- Your nail beds are wide or your fingers are short: almond does the flattering work more reliably
- You prefer short-to-medium length or work with natural nails: almond reads at any length, coffin needs canvas
- You type all day, use your hands constantly, or want press-ons that fit across a wide range of nail bed shapes
- Chrome, floral, or soft French is your go-to finish : almond's curved surface handles all three better
- You want something aligned with where the dominant 2026 aesthetic is heading: soft almond and modern almond are the shapes nail artists are building this year's biggest trends on

**Choose coffin if:**
- Your fingers are long and proportionate and you want the architectural silhouette that length earns
- You are going medium-to-long: coffin needs that length to establish its defining taper-to-flat sequence
- Ombré, graphic French, or bold statement art is your priority: the flat tip gives gradients more room and geometric designs a clean edge
- Drama is the point: coffin reads bolder, more fashion-forward, more TikTok-ready for statement sets
- You are wearing extensions rather than natural nails and can give the shape the structural support its corners need

And if the shape you have been eyeing on your feed looks like neither quite fits? Ask for the modern almond. It is the shape blurring the line between both in 2026, more durable than either extreme, and exactly what most people pointing to a screenshot are actually trying to order.

